reviews.text:
1. Biggest red flag: they check my cat’s fur using a shared comb - wiped by a thin paper. It passed fleas to my cat later, a nightmare;
2. My cat is in door 100% and loves to play with me, that week he’s not playful nor active, and I think he might have a fever. The vet confirmed it too. Did X-ray, urinalysis and blood work. After hours we got the blood results, then the vet told us she cannot read the blood report - then why order a blood report in the first place?
3. After $880, our cat is under severe stress and we still don’t know what’s wrong. Went home with antibiotics and painkillers;
4. Before we left, the cashier made a mistake by pressing one more 0 to the total- we were charged $8800 in my discover card. To fix this issue I had to use another card;
5. Luckily, three weeks later my cat recovered by himself. We just need to go to another vet to treat the flea passed from the shared comb. The flea spread to us too. Took another whole month to recover.

Never again will we go to this place. Nice exterior but worst vet service we’ve seen.
